(Bug #131: a call whose result has no declared type takes its type from the
 declaration it initialises, written directly or with arguments, so the
 text appends to a list as text and not as its address.)

To 'opaque label'. Return "hi".

To 'opaque word' with a number called ignored. Return "there".

a text called saved is 'opaque label'.
a text called other is 'opaque word' of 0.
a list called items is [].
append saved to items.
append other to items.
Print items.
Print element 2 of items.
